   "subject": "Debugging through the mirtCAT() function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Phil,<br><br>I was debugging mirtCAT() function using debug(mirtCAT) command to see how the next item selection works in case of multi dimensional items using Drule.<div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LSAT6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data_LSAT6 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> expand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LSAT6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>mod_LSAT6 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data_LSAT6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>debug</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mirtCAT</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">CATdesign</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirtCAT</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NULL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mod_LSAT6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">start_item </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Drule&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> criteria </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Drule&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ML&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">design_elements </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> local_pattern </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>While I was debugging it I came across Drule function which using ComputeCritera function internally. I need to go inside this function to see which parameters are taking which values.</div><div><br></div><div>Do you have any suggestions for me to how to debug an internal c++ function in R.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I know that I can not do it using RStudio. I have to use R from command line. I am doing that too; however it is not working it is throwing errors.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://r-pkgs.had.co.nz/src.html#src-debugging\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r-pkgs.had.co.nz/src.html%23src-debugging&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475531075000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DmljCaAvj2zAgUNQS1T8B\">http://r-pkgs.had.co.nz/src.html#src-debugging<br></a></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I tries starting R from command prompt by using this command R --debugger=gdb</div><div><br></div><div>but it says:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;line-height:16.8999996185303px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">unknown option </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;--debugger=gdb&#39;</span></div></code></div><br></span><br></div><div><span style=\"line-height:16.8999996185303px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I have downloaded the gcc compiler and it works fine when I am compiling separate c++ files from command prompt.</font></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:16.8999996185303px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:16.8999996185303px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> </font></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:16.8999996185303px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I only need to ask how do you do it when you are building a R packages which has c++ functions inside,( if in case you are going wrong ) how do you debug them?\r\n\r\n\r\nThank you very much,\r\n\r\nIrshad</font></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;line-height:16.8999996185303px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><br></span></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
