    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Wednesday, August 26, 2015 at 8:04:52 PM UTC+5:30, Phil Chalmers wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">This is largely outside what I know and practice. I never really use the gcc debugger, and would rather just print elements to the console if need be (I&#39;ve never found those debuggers to be terribly useful anyway). Might be better to post a Q like this on stack overflow.<div><br></div><div>Phil</div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Aug 26, 2015 at 8:52 AM, Irshad Mujawar <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">irshadmuj...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Phil,<br><br>I was debugging mirtCAT() function using debug(mirtCAT) command to see how the next item selection works in case of multi dimensional items using Drule.<div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LSAT6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data_LSAT6 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> expand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LSAT6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>mod_LSAT6 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data_LSAT6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><spa